1. Download a sample vulnerability scan report template from the OWASP website and review its main sections (Executive Summary, Findings, Recommendations, Appendix).
=>OWASP (especially the Web Security Testing Guide – WSTG Reporting section) does not publish one rigid “official PDF template,” but it strongly recommends a clear structure that separates business and technical audiences. Typical main sections are:
Executive Summary — High-level overview for managers: overall risk, key business impacts, and strategic recommendations (little or no technical jargon).
Findings — Detailed technical section: summary table of issues + per-finding description, risk rating, evidence/proof-of-concept, and impact.
Recommendations / Remediation — Clear, actionable guidance the development or operations team can follow.
Appendix — Supporting material (methodology, tools used, risk-rating definitions, scope, version history, etc.).

